  "interpretation": "A rigid-translation primitive (the simplest shared 'move a selected object' mechanic), params re-fit per game from few observations, was tested as the offline->live bridge. If exact_match is ~0 across games, the games' dynamics are NOT clean translations at the 64x64 PIXEL representation (cell=1: logical-cell detection found no downsample) -- objects are multi-color sprites that reflect (ar25), push (ka59), or redraw, not rigid color translations. The bridge then needs (a) an OBJECT-CENTRIC representation (segment sprites, track them as objects) so primitives are clean, AND (b) a LIBRARY of primitives (translate/reflect/push/toggle), not one. This is the shared root cause across all three probes (seeding, whole-engine LOGO, this): the binding constraint is induction quality, which is gated by the state REPRESENTATION.",
